# attestor
ATTESTOR_NODE_ID - identifier of this attestor node within the participant set
ATTESTOR_REGION - region label this node reports in health
ATTESTOR_LISTEN_ADDR - host:port the attestor API listens on
ATTESTOR_PEER_LISTEN_ADDR - host:port the peer transport listens on
ATTESTOR_PEERS - comma-separated id=host:port list of the other attestor nodes
ATTESTOR_NODE_KEY_FILE - path to the node key file (32 raw bytes or 64 hex characters) that encrypts the share store
ATTESTOR_DATA_DIR - directory holding the encrypted share store
ATTESTOR_CEREMONY - true enables keys.import for the operator during a ceremony window
ATTESTOR_CHAIN_ID - EVM chain id every decoded transaction is pinned to
ATTESTOR_JWKS_URL - identity provider JWKS endpoint used to verify user tokens
ATTESTOR_JWT_ISSUER - expected issuer of user tokens
ATTESTOR_JWT_AUDIENCE - expected audience of user tokens
ATTESTOR_POLICY_FILE - path to the default signing policy
ATTESTOR_TLS_CERT_FILE - path to this node's TLS certificate
ATTESTOR_TLS_KEY_FILE - path to this node's TLS private key
ATTESTOR_TLS_CA_FILE - path to the CA bundle that authenticates peers and the gateway
ATTESTOR_OPERATOR_CA_FILE - path to the CA bundle that authenticates the operator identity
ATTESTOR_BACKUP_KEY_FILE - path to the key file (32 raw bytes or 64 hex characters) that encrypts store snapshots
ATTESTOR_BACKUP_DIR - directory where encrypted store snapshots are written
ATTESTOR_RPC_URL - chain RPC endpoint used to read nonces and binding state

# gateway
NODE_ENV - runtime mode of the gateway: development, test or production
PORT - TCP port the gateway HTTP server listens on
LOG_LEVEL - gateway log verbosity
CORS_ORIGINS - comma-separated browser origins allowed to call the gateway, with single-level wildcard subdomains
SUPABASE_URL - Supabase project URL whose published JWKS verifies user access tokens
DATABASE_URL - connection string of the gateway's wallet database
DATABASE_POOL_MAX - maximum connections in the gateway's database pool
WALLET_MASTER_KEY - base64 32-byte key that encrypts legacy wallet key envelopes at rest
WALLET_MASTER_KEY_VERSION - version number of the active wallet master key
HYPERPAXEER_CHAIN_ID - EVM chain id the gateway signs for
HYPERPAXEER_RPC_URL - EVM JSON-RPC endpoint used for reads and broadcasts
HYPERPAXEER_EXPLORER_URL - block explorer base URL returned to clients for transaction links
POLICY_MAX_TX_VALUE_WEI - per-transaction native value cap for standard wallets
POLICY_MAX_DAILY_VALUE_WEI - rolling daily native value cap for standard wallets
POLICY_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE - signing requests allowed per wallet per minute
FUNDED_TREASURY_PRIVATE_KEY - treasury signing key of the funded lane, disabled when unset
FUNDED_USDL_ADDRESS - USDL token contract used as funded-lane collateral
FUNDED_USDL_DECIMALS - decimals of the USDL token
FUNDED_GAS_REFILL_THRESHOLD_WEI - native balance below which a funded wallet is topped up
FUNDED_GAS_REFILL_AMOUNT_WEI - native amount sent per funded-wallet top-up
FUNDED_EVALUATOR_INTERVAL_MS - tick interval of the funded drawdown evaluator
PAXSCAN_API_URL - explorer API base used to value funded wallets
PAXSCAN_TIMEOUT_MS - timeout of one explorer API request
PAXSCAN_CACHE_TTL_MS - lifetime of cached explorer valuations
FUNDED_BALANCE_READ_QUORUM - number of RPC reads sampled per funded balance read
FUNDED_DAILY_RESET_UTC_HOUR - UTC hour at which the funded daily drawdown window resets
API_WORKERS - number of gateway worker processes
AGENT_JWT_SECRET - HS256 secret that signs gateway-minted agent tokens, agent lane disabled when unset
AGENT_TOKEN_TTL_SECONDS - lifetime of an agent token
AGENT_CHALLENGE_TTL_SECONDS - lifetime of an agent authentication challenge
AGENT_DEFAULT_FROZEN - whether a newly seen agent principal starts frozen
AGENT_DEFAULT_MODE - initial mode of a newly seen agent principal
AGENT_BIND_OWNER_FROM_DID - whether an agent is bound to the owner named in its DID label
AGENT_DEFAULT_MAX_TX_VALUE_WEI - default per-transaction native value cap for agent wallets
AGENT_DEFAULT_MAX_DAILY_VALUE_WEI - default rolling daily native value cap for agent wallets
AGENT_DEFAULT_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE - default signing requests per agent per minute
AGENT_DEFAULT_MAX_APPROVE_WEI - default cap on ERC-20 approval amounts for agent wallets
LAYERX_VAULT_ADDRESS - LayerX custody vault contract targeted by agent deposit actions
LAYER_X_DB_URI - read-only connection string of the LayerX sequencer database
ACTION_CONFIRMATIONS - block confirmations before an agent action transaction is final
ACTION_RECEIPT_TIMEOUT_MS - maximum wait for one agent action receipt
ACTION_WORKER_INTERVAL_MS - tick interval of the agent action worker
ACTION_RECONCILE_INTERVAL_MS - sweep interval of the agent action reconciler
ACTION_FEE_BUMP_PERCENT - fee increase applied when replacing a stuck agent action transaction
LAYERX_SYNC_INTERVAL_MS - interval of the LayerX mirror sync worker
NEXT_PUBLIC_PAXEER_WALLET_API - wallet gateway base URL used by the demo
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL - Supabase project URL used by the demo for sign-in
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY - Supabase publishable key used by the demo for sign-in
NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_REDIRECT_URL - sign-in callback URL of the demo
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL - public origin of the demo used for page metadata
